  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "HAW3",
      "assessment": "PASS",
      "reason": "Checked the exact PlainIff ratio direction and q versus q^-1. The original global characters kill Weil-inertia commutators; the finite inertia image makes each commutator matrix semisimple, giving identity and then scalar inertia by irreducibility. Frobenius eigenline forces rank-one constituents. Generic unlinked singleton classification and zero monodromy prove full TypePlain and SphUnl under the expressly retained local foundations."
    },
    {
      "claim": "HAW4",
      "assessment": "PASS",
      "reason": "The retained contragredient/Gelfand-Kazhdan and field-transfer laws give inverse transported characters. Reversing the pair restores the exact forbidden ratio. The continuous local field isomorphism preserves valuation ring, units, uniformizer up to a unit, and residue cardinality; only quotient unramifiedness is used, so ramified individual characters remain allowed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "HAW5",
      "assessment": "PASS",
      "reason": "The actual same YOf decomposition and supplied PartLinkAlt give the same part and cusp. Outside V.S prime sphericality gives TU; inside s.S away from ell and v0 the place lies in St. Updating one local-component family member handles every component, and TypeForAlt retains every Teichmuller family/every IsRecT. ConjTor handles the other conjugate place. The exceptional v0 and exact V.S prime=s.S scope remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "claim": "HAW6",
      "assessment": "PASS",
      "reason": "BCS8 strict generic-unitary exponents and support uniqueness force every segment to be length one under Unl. The central-character norm-one compactness argument gives one global twist chi=norm^(-b/n), chosen before the place. Its local uniformizer modulus q^(b/n) yields the stated single window center -b/n, with strict half-width and all support witnesses. Only the basic retained central-character and idele-class facts are used for unitarization."
    }
